# Ignore `Archive /` (archived snapshots)

The directory **`Archive /`** (note the trailing space in the folder name) holds old copies and is **not** part of the live site.

- Do **not** read, edit, grep, refactor, or “sync” files under `Archive /` unless the user **explicitly** asks to work on archived content.
- For site-wide updates (nav, mailto links, copy, assets, case studies), only change files at the repo root and in `assets/`, `css/`, `js/`, etc. — **never** the Archive tree by default.
- If the user says to ignore Archive or refers to “archived folder,” treat this rule as authoritative for the whole repo.
